issue : How to rank higher and avoid overpaying for the priority fees ?

solution: 


Solana’s scheduler uses a Priority Score to rank transactions in the queue. The formula looks like this:  $$\te


Priority Score = (Validator Reward * 1,000,000 ) / (Estimated Cost + 1)

$$Validator Reward: Mostly your Priority Fee.
Estimated Cost: Your requested CU Limit.


If you don't set a SetComputeUnitLimit, the network gives you a default (usually 200,000 CUs)

Scenario	      CU Limit.   	CU Price	Total Priority Fee
Default (Lazy)	200,000.     	1,000	     200,000 Lamports
Optimized (Pro)	1,100	        1,000.    	1,100 Lamports


The Trap: If you set a massive CU Limit (the denominator), your Priority Score actually drops unless you pay an even more massive price. A transaction asking for 1.4 million CUs is "heavier" for the block, so the validator demands a higher price to give it the same priority as a "light" transaction.

Tip : 
      Developers use Priority Fee APIs to "calculate" the price by looking at what other people are paying right now.
what to do ::===>>>

The "Optimal" Transaction Strategy:

** Simulate the transaction to find actual CU usage.

**. Set Limit to Usage + 10% safety margin.

**.  Get Price from a recent fee API.

**.   Send both instructions in one transaction.

This ensures you are the first in line while paying the least amount of SOL possible.
